# Class File Organization

- Keep exactly one top-level class per `.cs` file.
- Name each file exactly as its class name.
- Place related classes into feature-oriented folders (for example `Settings/Colors`).
- When adding new classes, create folders as needed to keep files grouped by responsibility.
- Avoid multi-class utility dumps; split them into focused files.
